 Tool results are truncated to 2000 characters during serialization. Content beyond that limit is replaced with a marker indicating how many characters were truncated. This keeps summarization requests within reasonable token budgets, since tool results (especially from `read` and `bash`) are typically the largest contributors to context size.
 
+## Semantic boundary requests
+
+`ctx.requestCompaction` enters the same compaction backend with reason `semantic`, without aborting the active parent. During a run, Pi consumes the request after the full assistant/tool-result batch and before the next provider call. Idle requests use the same pipeline and can continue from the persisted checkpoint. The request supplies custom instructions and a canonical custom-message continuation; it does not supply its own summary.
+
+Pi persists replacement context and the canonical message before continuing. A subagent finishing during compaction does not own a separate parent continuation: its messages remain queued or are persisted normally if already selected by the loop. No child cancellation or wait-for-child completion is required. The scheduler must not implement an additional resume prompt in its callbacks.
+
+`force:true` uses a zero recent-token retention budget for semantic preparation only. Standard manual, threshold and overflow behavior is unchanged. An empty or already-compacted history can still be ineligible. `autoResume:false` and default failure handling end the current loop; they do not prohibit later independent input. Cancellation reports `AbortError` and never resumes automatically, even with `resumeOnFailure:true`.
+
+Ordering regressions should block the compaction backend and inject a notification both before and during the block, then verify that no provider call uses old context, no notification is lost, and the checkpoint appears once before the automatic continuation. Also test cancellation in post-compaction hooks and accepted requests on a failing turn; each request must settle even if the next-turn hook is never reached.
+
+See [Extensions](extensions.md#request-compaction-without-aborting-the-agent) for the public API.
+
