+### Request compaction without aborting the agent
+
+Use `ctx.requestCompaction(options)` for a semantic phase boundary. Unlike `ctx.compact()`, it does not abort the parent run. Pi waits until the complete current tool batch is persisted, runs the standard compaction pipeline before the next provider request, persists the supplied custom message, and continues once. Background workers remain independent and their messages are retained.
+
+```typescript
+const request = ctx.requestCompaction({
+  customInstructions: "Retain the verified decisions and outstanding work.",
+  force: true,
+  continuation: {
+    customType: "task-checkpoint",
+    content: "The investigation is complete. Next: implement the verified fix.",
+    display: false,
+  },
+  autoResume: true,
+  resumeOnFailure: false,
+  onError(error) {
+    // AbortError means cancellation, which never automatically resumes.
+    console.error(error.message);
+  },
+});
+if (!request.accepted) {
+  // Another compaction owns the boundary. Do not fall back to ctx.compact().
+}
+```
+
+Record intent from a tool or `turn_end`, not `context` (which is too late for next-turn preparation). Idle commands and shortcuts use the same pipeline. `force` sets the recent-token retention budget to zero for this semantic preparation only; it does not change configured threshold/overflow budgets or make empty history compactable.
+
+`autoResume:false` ends the current loop before another provider call. Already-selected input is persisted; other queued messages remain queued. This is not a permanent session lock: later independent input or extension triggers can start another run. Failure pauses by default; `resumeOnFailure:true` opts into one continuation with the available context. Callback observers must not send another automatic resume prompt.
+
+The returned `cancel()` cancels pending intent or in-flight semantic compaction, not the parent agent. It returns false after terminal settlement. Accepted requests receive one terminal callback; cancellation uses `AbortError` and never triggers failure auto-resume. Cancellation after persistence cannot undo the saved compaction. Session replacement invalidates pending work.
+
+See [Compaction](compaction.md#semantic-boundary-requests) for ordering and persistence details.
+
